<title>ARGENTINA: Spain's Telefonica ups stake in Argentine branch.</title>
<headline>Spain's Telefonica ups stake in Argentine branch.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telefonica de Argentina said Thursday its parent company Telefonica de Espana has raised its stake in the Argentine unit in a deal with Argentina's  Techint.</p>
<p>The Spanish company bought from Techint an 8.3 percent stake in Cointel, a holding that controls Telefonica de Argentina, the Argentine company said in a letter to the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>It did not disclose the amount of the deal.</p>
<p>Spain's Telefonica also bought from Argentina's CEI Citicorp Holdings SA shares representing 0.2026 percent of Cointel's capital, Telefonica de Argentina said.</p>
<p>As a consequence of this deal, CEI trimmed its stake in Cointel to 50 percent.</p>
<p>((--Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650)</p>
